# Module: Installing, Configuring, and Managing SELinux on Ubuntu Linux

## Module Overview

Security-Enhanced Linux (SELinux) provides an additional layer of security by implementing **Mandatory Access Control (MAC)**. Unlike traditional Linux permissions, SELinux uses security policies and security contexts to control how users, applications, and services access system resources.

In this module, you will learn how to install and enable SELinux on Ubuntu Linux, configure its operating modes, manage security contexts, map Linux users to SELinux users, secure Apache Web Server resources, and understand the fundamentals of AppArmor.

---

# Learning Objectives

After completing this module, you will be able to:

* Install and enable SELinux on Ubuntu Linux.
* Configure SELinux operating modes.
* Understand the SELinux configuration file.
* View and manage security contexts.
* Configure SELinux users and user mappings.
* Secure Apache Web Server using SELinux.
* Troubleshoot common SELinux permission issues.
* Understand AppArmor architecture and profile management.

